{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AptabaseBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AptabaseBatchEncoder","modules":[{"name":"AptabaseEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"AptabaseBatchEncoder.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder.swift#L74"},"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AptabaseBatchEncoder"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:16AptabaseEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AptabaseBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which fills in the endpoint, the app key’s header field, this encoder and its limits:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let aptabase = try HTTPDestination.aptabase(","    appKey: appKey,  \/\/ from the app's Instructions page: A-EU-…, A-US-… or A-SH-…","    isDebug: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose events only Debug mode should show","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON array, of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":", of one event per record, oldest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first. Each event is an object of these members:"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"eventName","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"sessionId","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" the same way when its context has no session"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"props","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, flattened; left out when there are none"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"systemProps"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, ","type":"text"},{"code":"isDebug","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"sdkVersion","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601, in UTC with milliseconds"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"systemProps","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holds "},{"code":"osName","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"osVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"appVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"appBuildNumber","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"deviceModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s language and region ("},{"code":"en-US","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), each left out when the context has no value for it;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"isDebug","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as the encoder is made with; and "},{"code":"sdkVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which Aptabase requires, always"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A member longer than Aptabase takes (30 characters of the system’s name, 100 of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its version, 50 of the app’s version, 20 of its build and 100 of the device’s model, counted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in UTF-16) is left out and the event is sent without it, as Aptabase refuses the whole request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holding one. The encoder logs a notice the first time it leaves out each member."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: Aptabase has no member for a user or a device. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without "},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") is a session of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own: Aptabase takes no event without a session. A record a store recovers after a relaunch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its session, so it goes out in the session of its first send. The record’s vendor identifier, trace context and other context"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values aren’t sent. Aptabase counts users itself, from a hash of each request’s IP address and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"User-Agent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" header field with a salt it changes every day."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, and so is an element of an array. Aptabase stores a string, a number or a boolean as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property’s value, and only a placeholder for an object or array, so an object or array is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spread into a property per value it holds, named after its path, joined by "},{"code":".","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"cart.size","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"tags.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and a "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe; one whose event name is only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whitespace or over 60 characters; one with a property whose name, once flattened, is empty, only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whitespace or over 40 characters, whose string value is over 180 characters, or whose number is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"too large for Aptabase; one whose values flatten to one name; one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; one that holds a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON can’t; one whose timestamp is outside the years 1 to 9999, or more than 23 hours before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the batch is encoded; and one too large for a request ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseEncodingError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default, gives each a deadline 23 hours after its oldest record was tracked, and makes none for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a batch with no record it can write, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends nothing for it. Aptabase","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t remove duplicates, so a record sent again, after a retry whose answer was lost or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store’s redelivery, is counted twice. The bytes are the same for the same records on every run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8 bytes.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of Aptabase’s events API, so an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send events to an Aptabase app’s "},{"code":"POST \/api\/v0\/events","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/init(isDebug:plan:limit:now:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"]},{"anchor":"Type-Aliases","generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/Failure"]},{"anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"]},{"anchor":"Type-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding\/aptabasebatchencoder"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"references":{"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding/AptabaseBatchEncoder/requests(for:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding\/aptabasebatchencoder\/requests(for:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"requests","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"for","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchRequests","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13BatchRequestsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"AptabaseEncodingError","preciseIdentifier":"s:16AptabaseEncoding0aB5ErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"requests(for:)","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"text":" as the requests Aptabase takes, each within the encoder’s limit and with a deadline","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"23 hours after its oldest record was tracked, with the records left out of them.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/do